Original commit body from a0831afd193c01190b988c9690791f2a82040e5e:

_extract_use_aliases read three use-forms and every one of them is a DIRECT
child of use_declaration. A grouped list is not -- tree-sitter wraps it in a
scoped_use_list one level down -- so all three lookups missed and the whole
declaration registered nothing. The call edge is still emitted, so nothing
fails loudly; only its identity is wrong, and the module slot gets the
`external` sentinel while the whole path is crammed into the name slot,
matching no io_primitives row.

Replaced with a recursive walk of the use-tree, because a use-tree nests.
The prefix is read textually from the node start to the opening brace rather
than by enumerating node types, since a prefix may be an identifier, a
scoped_identifier, crate, self, super, or carry a leading `::`. Wildcards
abstain at every depth without suppressing their siblings.

A/B over five rust repos, cold, baseline asserted by grepping the runtime
file: 642 -> 754 io chains, +112, zero lost, and the `external` sentinel goes
to zero on both repos audited for it. just is unchanged and is reported.

The item's second question is answered NO: the fully-qualified miss does not
share this cause -- both arms are still 0 after this fix, because those call
sites have no use statement to expand. Filed separately, with the PHP
instance the cross-language sweep found.

